==============================================================================
1. Theorem 6 from the other side: 2^k -+ 1 = q^s with s >= 2, all k <= 1500
==============================================================================
perfect powers among 2^k - 1, 2^k + 1 (k <= 1500): [(3, 9, 3, 2)]
  -> the only unit cell with s >= 2, for ANY odd q, is (q,k,s) = (3,3,2).  Agrees with Theorem 6.

