3. Signed kernel: is -1/2 an eigenvalue?  det(I + R_e - R_o) = 0, primes 5 <= p < 300
   (their range: p < 100, det mod 2^61-1)
==============================================================================
  q : primes p < 300 (p not dividing 2q) with det(I + R_e - R_o) = 0
      (zero modulo two 31-bit primes; confirmed by exact Bareiss determinant for p <= 61)
    3: 60 of 60  (all)
    5: 5 of 59  yes = [11, 13, 17, 29, 31]   [of these, p | q-3: []]
    7: 3 of 59  yes = [11, 19, 23]   [of these, p | q-3: []]
    9: 2 of 60  yes = [5, 19]   [of these, p | q-3: []]
   11: 4 of 59  yes = [13, 19, 29, 31]   [of these, p | q-3: []]
   13: 6 of 59  yes = [5, 19, 31, 37, 41, 59]   [of these, p | q-3: [5]]
   15: 5 of 59  yes = [11, 17, 19, 43, 47]   [of these, p | q-3: []]
   17: 4 of 59  yes = [7, 11, 47, 59]   [of these, p | q-3: [7]]
   31: 4 of 59  yes = [7, 13, 17, 23]   [of these, p | q-3: [7]]
   33: 4 of 59  yes = [5, 17, 19, 97]   [of these, p | q-3: [5]]
   63: 8 of 59  yes = [5, 11, 13, 17, 19, 29, 37, 191]   [of these, p | q-3: [5]]
   65: 3 of 58  yes = [17, 31, 193]   [of these, p | q-3: [31]]
  127: 5 of 59  yes = [11, 19, 29, 31, 37]   [of these, p | q-3: [31]]
  129: 6 of 59  yes = [5, 7, 11, 13, 19, 31]   [of these, p | q-3: [7]]
  NOTE (skeptic): K^-_p depends on q only through q mod p.  So 'the yes-list contains the primes
  dividing q - 3' is automatic (the matrix IS the q = 3 matrix there); it is not an independent
  confirmation of Proposition 7.  The remaining 'sporadic' primes are the content, and they are
  unexplained by the proposition.

